 "post": {
  "title": "The Big-No Trick That Gets You a Yes #shorts",
  "description": "Maya asks Kabir to help her move all weekend. He says no. Then: just the couch? Yes. Cialdini et al. (1975): only 17% of students agreed to chaperone juvenile delinquents on a day trip to the zoo, but 50% agreed after first refusing a much bigger request (two hours a week for two years as a counselor). The door-in-the-face technique. #psychology #shorts #persuasion #influence",
